==English==

===Etymology===
By analogy with a {{term|clam|lang=en}} closing itself.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inf=to [[clam]] [[up]]|clams up|clamming up|clammed up}}

# {{intransitive|idiomatic}} To become [[silent]]; to [[stop]] [[talking]], to [[shut up]].
#* '''1986''', [[w:Paul Chadwick|Paul Chadwick]], ''Concrete: Under the Desert Stars'', Dark Horse Books
#*: Maybe he … or she … was a witness who refused to clam up … a whistle blower …

====Synonyms====
* [[shut up]]

====Antonyms====
* [[talk]]

